abstract: >-
  The personal archive of Konstantin E. Tsiolkovsky (1857-1935) is held as
  fond 555 of the Archive of the Russian Academy of Sciences and has been
  scanned and put online, but without a queryable catalogue, full-text search
  or dataset. This repository contains a machine-readable catalogue of all
  2,019 files of the fond across its five inventories, covering 51,008 scans,
  together with the retrieval and measurement pipeline that produced it: a
  resumable downloader that resolves each file's real archival inventory and
  number from the scan paths, a page classifier that separates handwriting
  from typescript without a neural network, and a tool that scores
  transcriptions against published texts on Russian Wikisource. It further
  contains the dating of every file, collected from the archive's own cards
  and not previously available as a table, transcriptions of 98 files, and a
  measurement of how far reading error reaches on the fond's handwriting,
  obtained from texts the fond happens to hold twice.
